            "cwe_display": "CWE-502: Deserialization of Untrusted Data",
            "cwe_name": "Deserialization of Untrusted Data",
            "dataFlowTrace": "`imports(request)` → `import_handoff(upload)` → `import_handoff():35`\n\n- `portal/views.py:79-80` reads `request.FILES[\"bundle\"]`\n- That object is passed unchanged as `import_handoff(upload)`\n- `portal/services.py:35` calls `upload.read()` and sends those bytes to\n  `pickle.loads(...)`\n- Observed checks on the path:\n  - `request.method == \"POST\"`\n  - `request.FILES.get(\"bundle\")`\n- No content validation was found for file type, schema, signature, or allowed\n  object types before deserialization",
            "debateConsensus": "TP",
            "debateSummary": "- Review outcome recorded in the transcript: **1 true positive, 0 false positive**\n- The technical basis for the TP view was that `pickle.loads()` is reached with\n  attacker-controlled bytes from `request.FILES[\"bundle\"]`, and pickle can run\n  code during deserialization before later row handling occurs\n- No contrary technical argument appears in the provided transcript\n- Limitation: the debate evidence here is effectively an unchallenged\n  single-model review rather than a split panel",
            "end_line": 35,
            "fileSourceUrl": "https://github.com/caldova-io/support-portal/blob/1b68f887d82551e0d429c29bafbc3d11639c0700/portal/services.py#L35",
            "firstDetected": "2026-08-20T05:17:51.353Z",
            "fixDiff": "--- a/portal/services.py\n+++ b/portal/services.py\n@@ -31,12 +31,14 @@\n     return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n \n \n-def import_handoff(upload):\n-    rows = pickle.loads(upload.read())\n-    created = []\n-    for row in rows:\n-        subject = row.get(\"subject\", \"Delivery follow-up\")\n-        description = row.get(\"description\", \"\")\n+def import_handoff(upload):\n+    rows = __import__(\"json\").loads(upload.read().decode(\"utf-8\"))\n+    if not isinstance(rows, list) or not all(isinstance(row, dict) for row in rows):\n+        raise ValueError(\"bundle must be a JSON array of objects\")\n+    created = []\n+    for row in rows:\n+        subject = row.get(\"subject\", \"Delivery follow-up\")\n+        description = row.get(\"description\", \"\")\n         ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n             reference=row.get(\"reference\") or slugify(subject)[:18],\n             customer_key=row.get(\"customer_key\", \"walkup\"),\n",
            "fixStatus": "provided",
            "fixValidation": "strict",
            "fixes": [
              {
