            "annotatedSource": "def imports(request): # TAINT: request is untrusted HTTP input PRECOND: portal/urls.py:13 exposes this import endpoint directly with no authentication or permission wrapper HIST: portal/views.py is ranked a primary boundary with CWE-20, CWE-862, CWE-79, and CWE-22 hints\n    created = []\n    if request.method == \"POST\" and request.FILES.get(\"bundle\"): # TAINT: request.FILES[\"bundle\"] is user-supplied upload data PRECOND: only file presence is checked; there is no type, content, or size validation before deserialization\n        created = import_handoff(request.FILES[\"bundle\"]) # TAINT: uploaded bytes flow into import_handoff() in services.py:34-51 DATA-FLOW: that helper does upload.read() followed by pickle.loads(...), a classic unsafe deserialization path that can execute attacker-controlled payloads before validation ALLOC: upload.read() loads the entire file into memory first, so bundle size is attacker-controlled and can cause memory exhaustion ERRPATH: import_handoff() creates Ticket rows in a loop without a transaction, so a mid-import exception can leave a partial import committed\n        messages.success(request, f\"Imported {len(created)} tickets.\") # DATA-FLOW: success is reported only after unsafe deserialization and DB writes complete; len(created) reflects importer-controlled row count\n    return render(request, \"portal/imports.html\", {\"created\": created})",
