            "impact": "An unauthenticated or otherwise unauthorized caller can trigger the bulk import path and cause\ncreation of `Ticket` records. This can introduce unauthorized data into the ticketing system and\ninvoke any downstream processing that assumes imports are limited to privileged operators.",
            "prerequisites": "- The route `/imports/` must be reachable as configured in Django routing.\n- No external reverse-proxy rule, middleware, or deployment control can be enforcing access before\n  the request reaches this view.\n- This is application code in a normal Django view path, not an optional compiled component or\n  loadable extension.\n- The trust boundary is from an external HTTP client, including an anonymous user, into a database\n  write path that creates `Ticket` records.\n- The supplied threat model describes ticket persistence as a boundary where a remote\n  unauthenticated submitter or low-privilege user may cause ticket creation/import.\n- Related CVEs listed with the finding are not a close match for this pattern. The cited\n  `CVE-2007-4559` concerns archive path traversal, while this finding is an authorization check\n  issue.",
