            "severityRationale": "CVSS v3.1 base score 9.8 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H, confidence: medium) — AV:N (/imports/ is exposed in portal/urls.py and included at root in project/urls.py, so an external HTTP POST reaches views.imports and line 80); AC:L (the only enforced conditions are POST and presence of request.FILES[\"bundle\"], after which import_handoff() is invoked directly); PR:N (the view has no login, role, or permission check, and project/settings.py shows no global login-required middleware); UI:N (the attacker submits the upload directly with no separate victim action); S:U (import_handoff() and pickle.loads() run inside the same web application authority); C:H (services.py:35 deserializes attacker-supplied bytes with pickle.loads, and the annotated source states this can execute attacker-controlled payloads before validation, giving direct access to data available to the app process); I:H (the same deserialization path can directly execute attacker-controlled code and also create Ticket rows via Ticket.objects.create); A:H (attacker-controlled code execution in the app process can directly disrupt the service, and the path also reads the full uploaded file into memory).",
