              "description": {
                "text": "### Description\nIn `portal/views.py`, update `imports()` at lines 77-82 to reject anonymous users and require the `portal.add_ticket` permission before calling `import_handoff()`.\n\n### Suggested fix\n    return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n\n\ndef imports(request):\n    if not request.user.is_authenticated or not request.user.has_perm(\"portal.add_ticket\"):\n        return render(request, \"portal/imports.html\", {\"created\": []}, status=403)\n\n    created = []\n    if request.method == \"POST\" and request.FILES.get(\"bundle\"):\n        created = import_handoff(request.FILES[\"bundle\"])\n        messages.success(request, f\"Imported {len(created)} tickets.\")\n    return render(request, \"portal/imports.html\", {\"created\": created})\n\n### Rationale\nThe added guard enforces an authorization decision at the HTTP entry point before the bulk import path runs. Checking `request.user.is_authenticated` and `request.user.has_perm(\"portal.add_ticket\")` prevents unauthenticated or unauthorized callers from reaching the ticket-creation code, so the import action is no longer exposed as an unrestricted write operation.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, send a POST to `/imports/` with a `bundle` file while not logged in, or while logged in as a user without `portal.add_ticket`; the request reaches `import_handoff()` and creates tickets. After the change, the same requests should return HTTP 403 and create no `Ticket` rows. A logged-in user with `portal.add_ticket` should still be able to POST a valid bundle and receive the normal import success message."
              }
