            "impact": "A sufficiently large upload can cause the worker process to allocate memory proportional to the\nbundle size. Depending on deployment limits and available memory, this can lead to request\nfailures, worker termination, or reduced service availability.",
            "prerequisites": "- An attacker must be able to send a POST request to `/imports/` with a `bundle` file.\n- The reachable path is repo-visible and mapped from URL routing.\n- No `@login_required`, permission wrapper, or repo-visible upload-size setting was found for\n  this endpoint.\n- This is regular application code in the web service, not an optional extension.\n- The trust boundary crossed is **network client → server memory/deserialization path**.\n- The project threat model describes the service as network-facing and processing untrusted input.\n- The listed CVEs are adjacent rather than direct matches:\n  - `CVE-2017-18342` and `CVE-2024-27351` are deserialization-related and fit the same import\n    surface.\n  - No listed CVE is a direct analogue for this specific unbounded memory-read pattern.",
