              "description": {
                "text": "### Description\nIn portal/urls.py at line 10, remove the route that exposes views.ticket_detail on /tickets/<int:ticket_id>/ until the handler enforces object-level authorization for the requested ticket.\n\n### Suggested fix\n    path(\"\", views.inbox, name=\"inbox\"),\n    path(\"tickets/new/\", views.new_ticket, name=\"new_ticket\"),\n    path(\"tickets/search/\", views.search, name=\"search\"),\n    path(\"tickets/<int:ticket_id>/reply/\", views.reply, name=\"reply\"),\n    path(\"tickets/<int:ticket_id>/attachments/\", views.upload_attachment, name=\"upload_attachment\"),\n    path(\"imports/\", views.imports, name=\"imports\"),\n\n### Rationale\nDeleting the route removes the network entry point that accepts an attacker-chosen ticket_id and dispatches to the detail handler without any ticket ownership check. Without a reachable route, callers can no longer retrieve arbitrary Ticket objects through this direct object reference path.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, request GET /tickets/1/ (or another valid numeric ticket ID) and observe that the application reaches views.ticket_detail and returns the ticket detail page when the record exists. After the change, the same request should no longer dispatch to that handler and should return the framework's not-found response for the removed route."
              }
            }
