              "fixDiff": "--- a/portal/views.py\n+++ b/portal/views.py\n@@ -42,15 +42,16 @@\n     return render(request, \"portal/search.html\", {\"term\": term, \"results\": results})\n \n \n-def ticket_detail(request, ticket_id):\n-    ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n-    return render(request, \"portal/detail.html\", {\n-        \"ticket\": ticket,\n-        \"reply_form\": ReplyForm(initial={\"status\": ticket.status}),\n-        \"attachment_form\": AttachmentForm(),\n-        \"next_steps\": allowed_statuses(ticket.status),\n-        \"due_at\": response_due_at(ticket),\n-    })\n+def ticket_detail(request, ticket_id):\n+    customer_key = current_customer(request)\n+    ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id, customer_key=customer_key)\n+    return render(request, \"portal/detail.html\", {\n+        \"ticket\": ticket,\n+        \"reply_form\": ReplyForm(initial={\"status\": ticket.status}),\n+        \"attachment_form\": AttachmentForm(),\n+        \"next_steps\": allowed_statuses(ticket.status),\n+        \"due_at\": response_due_at(ticket),\n+    })\n \n \n def reply(request, ticket_id):",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn portal/views.py, update ticket_detail() at lines 45-46 to derive the caller's customer context with current_customer(request) and scope the Ticket lookup by both id and customer_key instead of id alone.\n\n### Suggested fix\n    return render(request, \"portal/search.html\", {\"term\": term, \"results\": results})\n\n\ndef ticket_detail(request, ticket_id):\n    customer_key = current_customer(request)\n    ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id, customer_key=customer_key)\n    return render(request, \"portal/detail.html\", {\n        \"ticket\": ticket,\n        \"reply_form\": ReplyForm(initial={\"status\": ticket.status}),\n        \"attachment_form\": AttachmentForm(),\n        \"next_steps\": allowed_statuses(ticket.status),\n        \"due_at\": response_due_at(ticket),\n    })\n\n\ndef reply(request, ticket_id):\n\n### Rationale\nScoping the ORM query by the request's customer_key binds the object fetch to the same tenant discriminator used elsewhere in the view layer. A ticket with a mismatched customer_key will no longer be returned, so an attacker-supplied ticket_id is treated as data within that customer's subset rather than as a global object reference.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, request /tickets/<other_customer_ticket_id>/ with a cookie containing a different customer_key and observe that the other customer's ticket detail page is rendered. After the change, repeat the same request and expect a 404 response, while a request for a ticket whose customer_key matches current_customer(request) still renders normally.",
