            "debateSummary": "- True positive: 1 model\n- False positive: 0 models\n\nKey points raised for the finding:\n- `customer_key` flows from unpickled row data directly into `Ticket.customer_key`\n- threat-model context describes `customer_key` as an authorization-critical tenant discriminator\n- reachability analysis found a public HTTP path through `/imports/` with no code-level auth check\n\nCounterpoint raised:\n- other parts of the application also appear to trust client-controlled tenant identifiers, so this\n  may reflect a broader application design pattern rather than an isolated import-only defect\n\nUnresolved point:\n- the debate transcript provided here is effectively single-model and unchallenged, so the count is\n  limited even though the recorded consensus is `TP`.",
