            "impact": "An uploaded bundle can assign imported tickets to arbitrary customer buckets or queues by choosing\nthe persisted `customer_key`. If later list, read, or workflow operations trust that field, tickets\nmay be misrouted, mixed across tenants, or associated with incorrect ownership metadata.",
            "prerequisites": "- An attacker must be able to reach the `/imports/` endpoint or another caller of\n  `import_handoff()`.\n- The path is part of the default Python web service, not an optional compiled extension.\n- The attacker must be able to upload a crafted bundle whose unpickled rows include a chosen\n  `customer_key`.\n- A meaningful security boundary exists only if downstream code uses `Ticket.customer_key` for\n  tenant isolation, queue placement, or ownership decisions.\n- The threat model does address this pattern: it describes `Ticket.customer_key` as a plain string\n  tenant discriminator and calls downstream trust in that field a broken-access-control hotspot.\n- The listed CVE references are mostly adjacent classes such as unsafe deserialization, SQL\n  injection, and traversal; this finding is not a direct variant of a cited CVE in the provided\n  material.",
            "recommendation": {
              "codeAfter": "    return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n\n\ndef import_handoff(upload, customer_key=\"walkup\"):\n    rows = pickle.loads(upload.read())\n    created = []\n    for row in rows:\n        subject = row.get(\"subject\", \"Delivery follow-up\")\n        description = row.get(\"description\", \"\")\n        ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n            reference=row.get(\"reference\") or slugify(subject)[:18],\n            customer_key=customer_key,\n            customer_name=row.get(\"customer_name\", \"Caldova customer\"),\n            delivery_address=row.get(\"delivery_address\", \"Unknown route\"),\n            robot_unit=row.get(\"robot_unit\", \"RB-000\"),\n            subject=subject,\n            description=description,\n            priority=priority_for(subject, description),\n        )\n        created.append(ticket)\n    return created\r",
              "codeBefore": "    return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n\n\ndef import_handoff(upload):\n    rows = pickle.loads(upload.read())\n    created = []\n    for row in rows:\n        subject = row.get(\"subject\", \"Delivery follow-up\")\n        description = row.get(\"description\", \"\")\n        ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n            reference=row.get(\"reference\") or slugify(subject)[:18],\n            customer_key=row.get(\"customer_key\", \"walkup\"),\n            customer_name=row.get(\"customer_name\", \"Caldova customer\"),\n            delivery_address=row.get(\"delivery_address\", \"Unknown route\"),\n            robot_unit=row.get(\"robot_unit\", \"RB-000\"),\n            subject=subject,\n            description=description,\n            priority=priority_for(subject, description),\n        )\n        created.append(ticket)\n    return created\r",
              "fixDiff": "--- a/portal/services.py\n+++ b/portal/services.py\n@@ -31,21 +31,21 @@\n     return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n \n \n-def import_handoff(upload):\n-    rows = pickle.loads(upload.read())\n-    created = []\n-    for row in rows:\n-        subject = row.get(\"subject\", \"Delivery follow-up\")\n-        description = row.get(\"description\", \"\")\n-        ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n-            reference=row.get(\"reference\") or slugify(subject)[:18],\n-            customer_key=row.get(\"customer_key\", \"walkup\"),\n-            customer_name=row.get(\"customer_name\", \"Caldova customer\"),\n-            delivery_address=row.get(\"delivery_address\", \"Unknown route\"),\n-            robot_unit=row.get(\"robot_unit\", \"RB-000\"),\n-            subject=subject,\n-            description=description,\n-            priority=priority_for(subject, description),\n-        )\n+def import_handoff(upload, customer_key=\"walkup\"):\n+    rows = pickle.loads(upload.read())\n+    created = []\n+    for row in rows:\n+        subject = row.get(\"subject\", \"Delivery follow-up\")\n+        description = row.get(\"description\", \"\")\n+        ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n+            reference=row.get(\"reference\") or slugify(subject)[:18],\n+            customer_key=customer_key,\n+            customer_name=row.get(\"customer_name\", \"Caldova customer\"),\n+            delivery_address=row.get(\"delivery_address\", \"Unknown route\"),\n+            robot_unit=row.get(\"robot_unit\", \"RB-000\"),\n+            subject=subject,\n+            description=description,\n+            priority=priority_for(subject, description),\n+        )\n         created.append(ticket)\n     return created",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn portal/services.py, update import_handoff() at lines 34-48 so Ticket.customer_key is not read from each unpickled row. Accept a trusted customer_key argument for the import operation and persist that server-side value instead of row.get(\"customer_key\").\n\n### Suggested fix\n    return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n\n\ndef import_handoff(upload, customer_key=\"walkup\"):\n    rows = pickle.loads(upload.read())\n    created = []\n    for row in rows:\n        subject = row.get(\"subject\", \"Delivery follow-up\")\n        description = row.get(\"description\", \"\")\n        ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n            reference=row.get(\"reference\") or slugify(subject)[:18],\n            customer_key=customer_key,\n            customer_name=row.get(\"customer_name\", \"Caldova customer\"),\n            delivery_address=row.get(\"delivery_address\", \"Unknown route\"),\n            robot_unit=row.get(\"robot_unit\", \"RB-000\"),\n            subject=subject,\n            description=description,\n            priority=priority_for(subject, description),\n        )\n        created.append(ticket)\n    return created\r\n\n### Rationale\nUsing a caller-supplied trusted customer_key removes the tenant/queue discriminator from attacker-controlled bundle data. The imported rows can still provide descriptive fields, but the ownership field is derived outside the untrusted file so the bundle contents no longer decide which customer bucket receives the new tickets.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, upload a bundle containing row[\"customer_key\"] = \"other-tenant\" and observe that the created Ticket row stores customer_key=\"other-tenant\". After the change, call import_handoff() with a trusted customer_key such as \"walkup\" (or the caller's current tenant) using the same bundle and verify the created Ticket row stores only the trusted value, not the value embedded in the bundle.",
              "remediationSteps": {
                "description": "In portal/services.py, update import_handoff() at lines 34-48 so Ticket.customer_key is not read from each unpickled row. Accept a trusted customer_key argument for the import operation and persist that server-side value instead of row.get(\"customer_key\").",
                "rational": "Using a caller-supplied trusted customer_key removes the tenant/queue discriminator from attacker-controlled bundle data. The imported rows can still provide descriptive fields, but the ownership field is derived outside the untrusted file so the bundle contents no longer decide which customer bucket receives the new tickets.",
                "rationale": "Using a caller-supplied trusted customer_key removes the tenant/queue discriminator from attacker-controlled bundle data. The imported rows can still provide descriptive fields, but the ownership field is derived outside the untrusted file so the bundle contents no longer decide which customer bucket receives the new tickets.",
                "suggestedFix": "    return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n\n\ndef import_handoff(upload, customer_key=\"walkup\"):\n    rows = pickle.loads(upload.read())\n    created = []\n    for row in rows:\n        subject = row.get(\"subject\", \"Delivery follow-up\")\n        description = row.get(\"description\", \"\")\n        ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n            reference=row.get(\"reference\") or slugify(subject)[:18],\n            customer_key=customer_key,\n            customer_name=row.get(\"customer_name\", \"Caldova customer\"),\n            delivery_address=row.get(\"delivery_address\", \"Unknown route\"),\n            robot_unit=row.get(\"robot_unit\", \"RB-000\"),\n            subject=subject,\n            description=description,\n            priority=priority_for(subject, description),\n        )\n        created.append(ticket)\n    return created\r",
                "verification": "Before the change, upload a bundle containing row[\"customer_key\"] = \"other-tenant\" and observe that the created Ticket row stores customer_key=\"other-tenant\". After the change, call import_handoff() with a trusted customer_key such as \"walkup\" (or the caller's current tenant) using the same bundle and verify the created Ticket row stores only the trusted value, not the value embedded in the bundle."
              }
