            "annotatedSource": "def save_attachment(ticket, upload): # TAINT: ticket is a trusted Ticket model from get_object_or_404; upload is attacker-controlled UploadedFile from request.FILES via AttachmentForm at portal/views.py:70-72 PRECOND: caller only ensures a file object exists; there is no repo-visible validation of size, MIME type, extension, or filename policy before persistence\n    storage = FileSystemStorage(location=\"media/uploads\") # CONSTRAINT: storage root is the relative path media/uploads; files are segregated only by this directory, not by tenant or random subpath\n    name = storage.save(upload.name, upload) # TAINT: upload.name is client-controlled and is used as the storage key, allowing the uploader to influence the persisted filename/path under the upload root DATA-FLOW: the service delegates collision handling and path normalization entirely to FileSystemStorage; there is no app-level quarantine, randomization, or content scanning HIST: file ranking flags this sink as persisting attacker-controlled file metadata/path material\n    return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name) # DATA-FLOW: original_name and stored_name are persisted to Attachment (portal/models.py:35-39; max_length 180/240) without full_clean(), so oversized or unexpected names rely on backend behavior ERRPATH: if Attachment.objects.create raises after storage.save succeeds, the file remains on disk as an orphan because no cleanup or transaction spans lines 30-31",
