            "cwe_display": "CWE-434: Unrestricted Upload of File with Dangerous Type",
            "cwe_name": "Unrestricted Upload of File with Dangerous Type",
            "dataFlowTrace": "`upload_attachment()` → `save_attachment():30`\n\n- **Entry point:** `portal/views.py:68-74` `upload_attachment(request, ticket_id)`\n  - `form = AttachmentForm(request.POST, request.FILES)`\n  - `upload = form.cleaned_data[\"file\"]`\n- **Intermediate validation:**\n  - `request.method == \"POST\"`\n  - `form.is_valid()`\n  - `AttachmentForm` defines only `file = forms.FileField()`\n- **Flagged sink:** `portal/services.py:30`\n  - `upload.name` flows into `storage.save(upload.name, upload)`\n  - `upload` carries attacker-controlled bytes\n- **Observed gaps on this path:**\n  - no repo-visible extension allowlist\n  - no repo-visible MIME or content inspection\n  - no repo-visible file size limit\n  - no server-generated storage name before save",
            "debateConsensus": "TP",
            "debateSummary": "- **Models classifying true positive:** 1\n- **Models classifying false positive:** 0\n\nAvailable debate evidence contains a single model review, so there was no multi-model disagreement\nrecorded. The review stated that the code writes attacker-controlled file content to disk with no\ntype restrictions and noted that, in deployments serving media content, this can expose arbitrary\nhosted files or active content.\n\nThe same review also noted contextual limits: this is an attachment feature by design, and\n`FileSystemStorage` addresses traversal and overwrite handling more than dangerous-file-type policy.\nNo contrary model argued that the finding was a false positive.",
            "end_line": 30,
            "fileSourceUrl": "https://github.com/caldova-io/support-portal/blob/1b68f887d82551e0d429c29bafbc3d11639c0700/portal/services.py#L30",
            "firstDetected": "2026-08-20T05:18:31.828Z",
            "fixDiff": "--- a/portal/services.py\n+++ b/portal/services.py\n@@ -1,5 +1,8 @@\n-import pickle\n-from django.core.files.storage import FileSystemStorage\n+import os\n+import pickle\n+import uuid\n+from django.core.exceptions import ValidationError\n+from django.core.files.storage import FileSystemStorage\n from django.db import connection\n from django.template import Context, Template\n from django.utils.text import slugify\n@@ -25,10 +28,43 @@\n     return tpl.render(Context({\"ticket\": ticket, \"agent\": request.user, \"request\": request}))\n \n \n-def save_attachment(ticket, upload):\n-    storage = FileSystemStorage(location=\"media/uploads\")\n-    name = storage.save(upload.name, upload)\n-    return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n+def _validated_attachment_extension(upload):\n+    max_upload_size = 5 * 1024 * 1024\n+    allowed_signatures = {\n+        \".pdf\": (b\"%PDF-\",),\n+        \".png\": (b\"\\x89PNG\\r\\n\\x1a\\n\",),\n+        \".jpg\": (b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\",),\n+        \".jpeg\": (b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\",),\n+        \".txt\": tuple(),\n+    }\n+\n+    ext = os.path.splitext(upload.name)[1].lower()\n+    if ext not in allowed_signatures:\n+        raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\")\n+    if upload.size > max_upload_size:\n+        raise ValidationError(\"Attachment too large\")\n+\n+    header = upload.read(16)\n+    upload.seek(0)\n+\n+    if ext == \".txt\":\n+        try:\n+            header.decode(\"utf-8\")\n+        except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n+            raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\") from exc\n+        return ext\n+\n+    if not any(header.startswith(signature) for signature in allowed_signatures[ext]):\n+        raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\")\n+    return ext\n+\n+\n+\n+def save_attachment(ticket, upload):\n+    ext = _validated_attachment_extension(upload)\n+    storage = FileSystemStorage(location=\"media/uploads\")\n+    name = storage.save(f\"{uuid.uuid4().hex}{ext}\", upload)\n+    return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n \n \n def import_handoff(upload):\n",
            "fixStatus": "provided",
            "fixValidation": "strict",
            "fixes": [
              {
                "artifactChanges": [
                  {
                    "artifactLocation": {
                      "uri": "portal/services.py",
                      "uriBaseId": "SRCROOT"
                    },
                    "replacements": [
                      {
                        "deletedRegion": {
                          "endLine": 2,
                          "startLine": 1
                        },
                        "insertedContent": {
                          "text": "import os\nimport pickle\nimport uuid\nfrom django.core.exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom django.core.files.storage import FileSystemStorage\n"
                        }
                      },
                      {
                        "deletedRegion": {
                          "endLine": 31,
                          "startLine": 28
                        },
                        "insertedContent": {
                          "text": "def _validated_attachment_extension(upload):\n    max_upload_size = 5 * 1024 * 1024\n    allowed_signatures = {\n        \".pdf\": (b\"%PDF-\",),\n        \".png\": (b\"\\x89PNG\\r\\n\\x1a\\n\",),\n        \".jpg\": (b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\",),\n        \".jpeg\": (b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\",),\n        \".txt\": tuple(),\n    }\n\n    ext = os.path.splitext(upload.name)[1].lower()\n    if ext not in allowed_signatures:\n        raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\")\n    if upload.size > max_upload_size:\n        raise ValidationError(\"Attachment too large\")\n\n    header = upload.read(16)\n    upload.seek(0)\n\n    if ext == \".txt\":\n        try:\n            header.decode(\"utf-8\")\n        except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n            raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\") from exc\n        return ext\n\n    if not any(header.startswith(signature) for signature in allowed_signatures[ext]):\n        raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\")\n    return ext\n\n\n\ndef save_attachment(ticket, upload):\n    ext = _validated_attachment_extension(upload)\n    storage = FileSystemStorage(location=\"media/uploads\")\n    name = storage.save(f\"{uuid.uuid4().hex}{ext}\", upload)\n    return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ],
                "description": {
                  "markdown": "Define an explicit attachment policy in `save_attachment()` or earlier in the form/view layer:\n\n- allow only expected attachment types\n- enforce a maximum upload size\n- validate content against the allowed type set\n- generate a server-side storage name instead of using `upload.name`\n- store uploads in a location and serving path appropriate for untrusted content\n\nA concrete fix was prepared that adds a small allowlist, basic header checks, a size limit, and a\nUUID-based stored filename.",
                  "text": "Define an explicit attachment policy in `save_attachment()` or earlier in the form/view layer:"
                }
              }
            ],
            "function": "portal/services.py:save_attachment",
            "group": {
              "displayId": "G0002",
              "groupId": "agent-group-2",
              "memberCount": 2
            },
            "impact": "If the route is exposed and stored uploads are later served or processed in a sensitive context, an\nattacker can cause arbitrary files to be written under `media/uploads`. This may allow hosting of\nunexpected file types, storage of active content, or persistence of oversized or malformed files\nfor later consumption.\n\nThe filename is attacker-controlled at input, although Django `FileSystemStorage` performs path\nnormalization and collision handling rather than writing raw paths verbatim.",
            "prerequisites": "- The upload route must be reachable:\n  - `portal/urls.py:12` maps\n    `/tickets/<int:ticket_id>/attachments/` to `views.upload_attachment`\n- No repo-visible `@login_required` or permission decorator is present on that view\n- The attacker needs the ability to submit a multipart upload for an existing ticket ID\n- This is application code in the main Django app, not an optional extension\n- The trust boundary crossed is:\n  - network-supplied multipart file data and filename\n  - into filesystem storage and persistent attachment metadata\n- The threat model identifies attachment metadata persistence as a boundary and calls out\n  filename/path handling as a security-sensitive area\n- The code path is reachable according to the supplied routing and call graph evidence\n- Related historical reference:\n  - `CVE-2007-4559` is the closest listed pattern because it also involves attacker-controlled\n    file metadata, but this code path is not an archive-extraction case; it is closer to a generic\n    unrestricted upload pattern",
            "recommendation": {
              "codeAfter": "1: import os\n2: import pickle\n3: import uuid\n4: from django.core.exceptions import ValidationError\n5: from django.core.files.storage import FileSystemStorage\n6: from django.db import connection\n7: from django.template import Context, Template\n8: from django.utils.text import slugify\n// ...\n28:     return tpl.render(Context({\"ticket\": ticket, \"agent\": request.user, \"request\": request}))\n29:\n30:\n31: def _validated_attachment_extension(upload):\n32:     max_upload_size = 5 * 1024 * 1024\n33:     allowed_signatures = {\n34:         \".pdf\": (b\"%PDF-\",),\n35:         \".png\": (b\"\\x89PNG\\r\\n\\x1a\\n\",),\n36:         \".jpg\": (b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\",),\n37:         \".jpeg\": (b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\",),\n38:         \".txt\": tuple(),\n39:     }\n40:\n41:     ext = os.path.splitext(upload.name)[1].lower()\n42:     if ext not in allowed_signatures:\n43:         raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\")\n44:     if upload.size > max_upload_size:\n45:         raise ValidationError(\"Attachment too large\")\n46:\n47:     header = upload.read(16)\n48:     upload.seek(0)\n49:\n50:     if ext == \".txt\":\n51:         try:\n52:             header.decode(\"utf-8\")\n53:         except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n54:             raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\") from exc\n55:         return ext\n56:\n57:     if not any(header.startswith(signature) for signature in allowed_signatures[ext]):\n58:         raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\")\n59:     return ext\n60:\n61:\n62:\n63: def save_attachment(ticket, upload):\n64:     ext = _validated_attachment_extension(upload)\n65:     storage = FileSystemStorage(location=\"media/uploads\")\n66:     name = storage.save(f\"{uuid.uuid4().hex}{ext}\", upload)\n67:     return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n68:\n69:\n70: def import_handoff(upload):",
              "codeBefore": "1: import pickle\n2: from django.core.files.storage import FileSystemStorage\n3: from django.db import connection\n4: from django.template import Context, Template\n5: from django.utils.text import slugify\n// ...\n25:     return tpl.render(Context({\"ticket\": ticket, \"agent\": request.user, \"request\": request}))\n26:\n27:\n28: def save_attachment(ticket, upload):\n29:     storage = FileSystemStorage(location=\"media/uploads\")\n30:     name = storage.save(upload.name, upload)\n31:     return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n32:\n33:\n34: def import_handoff(upload):",
              "fixDiff": "--- a/portal/services.py\n+++ b/portal/services.py\n@@ -1,5 +1,8 @@\n-import pickle\n-from django.core.files.storage import FileSystemStorage\n+import os\n+import pickle\n+import uuid\n+from django.core.exceptions import ValidationError\n+from django.core.files.storage import FileSystemStorage\n from django.db import connection\n from django.template import Context, Template\n from django.utils.text import slugify\n@@ -25,10 +28,43 @@\n     return tpl.render(Context({\"ticket\": ticket, \"agent\": request.user, \"request\": request}))\n \n \n-def save_attachment(ticket, upload):\n-    storage = FileSystemStorage(location=\"media/uploads\")\n-    name = storage.save(upload.name, upload)\n-    return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n+def _validated_attachment_extension(upload):\n+    max_upload_size = 5 * 1024 * 1024\n+    allowed_signatures = {\n+        \".pdf\": (b\"%PDF-\",),\n+        \".png\": (b\"\\x89PNG\\r\\n\\x1a\\n\",),\n+        \".jpg\": (b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\",),\n+        \".jpeg\": (b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\",),\n+        \".txt\": tuple(),\n+    }\n+\n+    ext = os.path.splitext(upload.name)[1].lower()\n+    if ext not in allowed_signatures:\n+        raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\")\n+    if upload.size > max_upload_size:\n+        raise ValidationError(\"Attachment too large\")\n+\n+    header = upload.read(16)\n+    upload.seek(0)\n+\n+    if ext == \".txt\":\n+        try:\n+            header.decode(\"utf-8\")\n+        except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n+            raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\") from exc\n+        return ext\n+\n+    if not any(header.startswith(signature) for signature in allowed_signatures[ext]):\n+        raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\")\n+    return ext\n+\n+\n+\n+def save_attachment(ticket, upload):\n+    ext = _validated_attachment_extension(upload)\n+    storage = FileSystemStorage(location=\"media/uploads\")\n+    name = storage.save(f\"{uuid.uuid4().hex}{ext}\", upload)\n+    return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n \n \n def import_handoff(upload):",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn portal/services.py, add upload validation before save_attachment() persists the file at line 30: enforce a small allowlist of attachment types using extension and header-signature checks, reject oversized uploads, and replace the client-supplied storage name with a server-generated UUID-based filename.\n\n### Suggested fix\nimport os\nimport pickle\nimport uuid\nfrom django.core.exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom django.core.files.storage import FileSystemStorage\nfrom django.db import connection\nfrom django.template import Context, Template\nfrom django.utils.text import slugify\n    return tpl.render(Context({\"ticket\": ticket, \"agent\": request.user, \"request\": request}))\n\n\ndef _validated_attachment_extension(upload):\n    max_upload_size = 5 * 1024 * 1024\n    allowed_signatures = {\n        \".pdf\": (b\"%PDF-\",),\n        \".png\": (b\"\\x89PNG\\r\\n\\x1a\\n\",),\n        \".jpg\": (b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\",),\n        \".jpeg\": (b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\",),\n        \".txt\": tuple(),\n    }\n\n    ext = os.path.splitext(upload.name)[1].lower()\n    if ext not in allowed_signatures:\n        raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\")\n    if upload.size > max_upload_size:\n        raise ValidationError(\"Attachment too large\")\n\n    header = upload.read(16)\n    upload.seek(0)\n\n    if ext == \".txt\":\n        try:\n            header.decode(\"utf-8\")\n        except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n            raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\") from exc\n        return ext\n\n    if not any(header.startswith(signature) for signature in allowed_signatures[ext]):\n        raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\")\n    return ext\n\n\n\ndef save_attachment(ticket, upload):\n    ext = _validated_attachment_extension(upload)\n    storage = FileSystemStorage(location=\"media/uploads\")\n    name = storage.save(f\"{uuid.uuid4().hex}{ext}\", upload)\n    return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n\n\ndef import_handoff(upload):\n\n### Rationale\nThe change narrows accepted uploads to known attachment formats, rejects files that do not match the expected file signature or exceed the size limit, and prevents the client from controlling the stored filename. This reduces unrestricted file persistence and removes direct use of attacker-chosen path material as the storage key.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, submit POST /tickets/<id>/attachments/ with a multipart file such as shell.php or payload.html named by the client; the file is written into media/uploads and the attacker-controlled filename is used for storage. After the change, the same request should raise a validation error and no file should be created. A valid .png or .pdf under 5 MiB should still be accepted, but the stored filename should be a generated UUID plus the approved extension rather than the original client name.",
              "remediationSteps": {
                "description": "In portal/services.py, add upload validation before save_attachment() persists the file at line 30: enforce a small allowlist of attachment types using extension and header-signature checks, reject oversized uploads, and replace the client-supplied storage name with a server-generated UUID-based filename.",
                "rational": "The change narrows accepted uploads to known attachment formats, rejects files that do not match the expected file signature or exceed the size limit, and prevents the client from controlling the stored filename. This reduces unrestricted file persistence and removes direct use of attacker-chosen path material as the storage key.",
                "rationale": "The change narrows accepted uploads to known attachment formats, rejects files that do not match the expected file signature or exceed the size limit, and prevents the client from controlling the stored filename. This reduces unrestricted file persistence and removes direct use of attacker-chosen path material as the storage key.",
                "suggestedFix": "import os\nimport pickle\nimport uuid\nfrom django.core.exceptions import ValidationError\nfrom django.core.files.storage import FileSystemStorage\nfrom django.db import connection\nfrom django.template import Context, Template\nfrom django.utils.text import slugify\n    return tpl.render(Context({\"ticket\": ticket, \"agent\": request.user, \"request\": request}))\n\n\ndef _validated_attachment_extension(upload):\n    max_upload_size = 5 * 1024 * 1024\n    allowed_signatures = {\n        \".pdf\": (b\"%PDF-\",),\n        \".png\": (b\"\\x89PNG\\r\\n\\x1a\\n\",),\n        \".jpg\": (b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\",),\n        \".jpeg\": (b\"\\xff\\xd8\\xff\",),\n        \".txt\": tuple(),\n    }\n\n    ext = os.path.splitext(upload.name)[1].lower()\n    if ext not in allowed_signatures:\n        raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\")\n    if upload.size > max_upload_size:\n        raise ValidationError(\"Attachment too large\")\n\n    header = upload.read(16)\n    upload.seek(0)\n\n    if ext == \".txt\":\n        try:\n            header.decode(\"utf-8\")\n        except UnicodeDecodeError as exc:\n            raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\") from exc\n        return ext\n\n    if not any(header.startswith(signature) for signature in allowed_signatures[ext]):\n        raise ValidationError(\"Unsupported attachment type\")\n    return ext\n\n\n\ndef save_attachment(ticket, upload):\n    ext = _validated_attachment_extension(upload)\n    storage = FileSystemStorage(location=\"media/uploads\")\n    name = storage.save(f\"{uuid.uuid4().hex}{ext}\", upload)\n    return Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)\n\n\ndef import_handoff(upload):",
                "verification": "Before the change, submit POST /tickets/<id>/attachments/ with a multipart file such as shell.php or payload.html named by the client; the file is written into media/uploads and the attacker-controlled filename is used for storage. After the change, the same request should raise a validation error and no file should be created. A valid .png or .pdf under 5 MiB should still be accepted, but the stored filename should be a generated UUID plus the approved extension rather than the original client name."
              }
