            "function": "portal/services.py:TicketSearch.find",
            "impact": "A caller could search for common terms and receive up to 25 matching ticket rows across\ncustomers, including `id`, `reference`, `customer_name`, `subject`, `status`, and\n`priority`. This enables cross-tenant enumeration of ticket metadata and may disclose\nbusiness or customer information outside the intended tenant scope.",
            "prerequisites": "- The route `/tickets/search/` must be reachable to an attacker.\n- No unseen middleware, gateway, or external access control may add authorization before\n  `views.search` executes.\n- The application must contain tickets for multiple customers in `portal_ticket`.\n- This is part of the web application's normal URL routing, not an optional extension.\n- The trust boundary is public or low-privilege HTTP input crossing into tenant-scoped\n  ticket data.\n- The apparent attacker is a remote caller who can submit `q` to the search endpoint.\n- The project threat model identifies `Ticket.customer_key` as an authorization-critical\n  tenant discriminator and specifically calls out missing checks on reads keyed by this\n  field as a CWE-862 hotspot.\n\nRelated known-pattern note:\n- The provided reference is a generic CWE-862 KB pattern for missing authorization\n  checks. No function-specific CVE match was provided for this code path.",
