              "description": {
                "text": "### Description\nIn portal/services.py, update TicketSearch.find at lines 11-20 to require a customer scope, add a customer_key predicate to the SQL, and bind the search values as query parameters. In portal/views.py, update search() to pass current_customer(request) into TicketSearch.find instead of calling the search with only the user-controlled term.\n\n### Suggested fix\nclass TicketSearch:\n    def find(self, term, customer_key=None):\n        if not customer_key:\n            return []\n        pattern = f\"%{term}%\"\n        sql = (\n            \"select id, reference, customer_name, subject, status, priority \"\n            \"from portal_ticket \"\n            \"where customer_key = %s and (reference like %s \"\n            \"or customer_name like %s or delivery_address like %s) \"\n            \"order by updated_at desc limit 25\"\n        )\n        with connection.cursor() as cursor:\n            cursor.execute(sql, [customer_key, pattern, pattern, pattern])\n            return [dict(zip([col[0] for col in cursor.description], row))\n                    for row in cursor.fetchall()]\n\n\ndef render_agent_response(ticket, body, request):\n++ b/portal/views.py\n\n\ndef search(request):\n    term = request.GET.get(\"q\", \"\")\n    customer_key = current_customer(request)\n    results = TicketSearch().find(term, customer_key=customer_key) \\\n        if term and customer_key else []\n    return render(request, \"portal/search.html\", {\"term\": term, \"results\": results})\n\n### Rationale\nAdding customer_key to the query constrains results to the caller's tenant, so matching rows from other customers are not returned. Requiring the caller to supply the current customer scope makes the authorization boundary explicit, and bound SQL parameters keep the search term and tenant key treated as data rather than query text.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, send a request such as GET /tickets/search/?q=delivery while scoped to customer A (or without authentication if the route is public) and observe that the response can include ticket metadata for customer B. After the change, the same request should return only rows whose customer_key matches current_customer(request); if no customer_key is available, the result set should be empty."
              }
