            "aiGenerated": true,
            "annotatedSource": "def render_agent_response(ticket, body, request): # TAINT: ticket is a trusted Ticket model from get_object_or_404, body is attacker-controlled POST text from ReplyForm.cleaned_data['body'] at portal/views.py:60, and request is external HTTP state PRECOND: caller only validates form structure and status choice; the /tickets/<id>/reply/ route is exposed in portal/urls.py:11 with no repo-visible auth guard or template-safety checks HIST: file ranking flags this function as a highest-risk template-render sink\n    tpl = Template(body) # DATA-FLOW: Template(body) compiles user-supplied text as Django template source, enabling server-side template injection against the context provided below ERRPATH: malformed template syntax raises TemplateSyntaxError and portal/views.py:56-65 does not catch it, causing a request-level 500\n    return tpl.render(Context({\"ticket\": ticket, \"agent\": request.user, \"request\": request})) # DATA-FLOW: render exposes the full Ticket object, request.user, and request to attacker-authored template expressions, enabling server-side data disclosure and forged response content CONSTRAINT: downstream display uses note.body|linebreaks in templates/portal/detail.html:14, so HTML is autoescaped there; the primary risk is template-time data access, not direct raw HTML injection",
