              "codeBefore": "20:             return [dict(zip([col[0] for col in cursor.description], row)) for row in cursor.fetchall()]\n21:\n22:\n23: def render_agent_response(ticket, body, request):\n24:     tpl = Template(body)\n25:     return tpl.render(Context({\"ticket\": ticket, \"agent\": request.user, \"request\": request}))\n26:\n27:\n28: def save_attachment(ticket, upload):",
              "fixDiff": "--- a/portal/services.py\n+++ b/portal/services.py\n@@ -20,9 +20,8 @@\n             return [dict(zip([col[0] for col in cursor.description], row)) for row in cursor.fetchall()]\n \n \n-def render_agent_response(ticket, body, request):\n-    tpl = Template(body)\n-    return tpl.render(Context({\"ticket\": ticket, \"agent\": request.user, \"request\": request}))\n+def render_agent_response(ticket, body, request):\n+    return body\n \n \n def save_attachment(ticket, upload):",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn portal/services.py, replace render_agent_response() at lines 23-25 so it returns the submitted reply text directly instead of compiling body with Template() and rendering it with ticket, agent, and request context.\n\n### Suggested fix\n            return [dict(zip([col[0] for col in cursor.description], row)) for row in cursor.fetchall()]\n\n\ndef render_agent_response(ticket, body, request):\n    return body\n\n\ndef save_attachment(ticket, upload):\n\n### Rationale\nRemoving Template(body) stops attacker-controlled reply text from being parsed as Django template source. Returning the text as data prevents server-side evaluation of {{...}} and {%...%} expressions, so ticket and request objects are no longer exposed through template rendering.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, submit a reply body such as '{{ ticket.reference }} / {{ agent }}' to /tickets/<id>/reply/ and observe that the stored/rendered note contains values derived from server-side objects; malformed template syntax may also trigger a TemplateSyntaxError response. After the change, submit the same payload and verify that the note contains the literal characters '{{ ticket.reference }} / {{ agent }}' and that no server-side template evaluation occurs.",
              "remediationSteps": {
                "description": "In portal/services.py, replace render_agent_response() at lines 23-25 so it returns the submitted reply text directly instead of compiling body with Template() and rendering it with ticket, agent, and request context.",
                "rational": "Removing Template(body) stops attacker-controlled reply text from being parsed as Django template source. Returning the text as data prevents server-side evaluation of {{...}} and {%...%} expressions, so ticket and request objects are no longer exposed through template rendering.",
                "rationale": "Removing Template(body) stops attacker-controlled reply text from being parsed as Django template source. Returning the text as data prevents server-side evaluation of {{...}} and {%...%} expressions, so ticket and request objects are no longer exposed through template rendering.",
