              "fixDiff": "--- a/portal/services.py\n+++ b/portal/services.py\n@@ -9,15 +9,16 @@\n \n class TicketSearch:\n     def find(self, term):\n-        sql = (\n-            \"select id, reference, customer_name, subject, status, priority \"\n-            f\"from portal_ticket where reference like '%{term}%' \"\n-            f\"or customer_name like '%{term}%' or delivery_address like '%{term}%' \"\n-            \"order by updated_at desc limit 25\"\n-        )\n-        with connection.cursor() as cursor:\n-            cursor.execute(sql)\n-            return [dict(zip([col[0] for col in cursor.description], row)) for row in cursor.fetchall()]\n+        pattern = f\"%{term}%\"\n+        sql = (\n+            \"select id, reference, customer_name, subject, status, priority \"\n+            \"from portal_ticket where reference like %s \"\n+            \"or customer_name like %s or delivery_address like %s \"\n+            \"order by updated_at desc limit 25\"\n+        )\n+        with connection.cursor() as cursor:\n+            cursor.execute(sql, [pattern, pattern, pattern])\n+            return [dict(zip([col[0] for col in cursor.description], row)) for row in cursor.fetchall()]\n \n \n def render_agent_response(ticket, body, request):",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn portal/services.py, update TicketSearch.find() around lines 12-19 to stop formatting term into the SQL string. Build a single LIKE pattern value and pass it to cursor.execute() as bound parameters for the three predicates.\n\n### Suggested fix\nclass TicketSearch:\n    def find(self, term):\n        pattern = f\"%{term}%\"\n        sql = (\n            \"select id, reference, customer_name, subject, status, priority \"\n            \"from portal_ticket where reference like %s \"\n            \"or customer_name like %s or delivery_address like %s \"\n            \"order by updated_at desc limit 25\"\n        )\n        with connection.cursor() as cursor:\n            cursor.execute(sql, [pattern, pattern, pattern])\n            return [dict(zip([col[0] for col in cursor.description], row)) for row in cursor.fetchall()]\n\n\ndef render_agent_response(ticket, body, request):\n\n### Rationale\nBound parameters send the search term to the database as data instead of SQL syntax. This prevents quote, comment, and operator characters in term from changing the structure of the WHERE clause while preserving LIKE matching behavior.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, request /tickets/search/?q=' OR 1=1 -- can change the WHERE clause and return rows unrelated to the intended search. After the change, the same request should be treated as a literal search string, the generated SQL text should remain unchanged except for placeholders, and results should only match rows containing the literal payload text if any exist.",
