            "dataFlowTrace": "`GET /` → URL pattern `\"\"` in `portal/urls.py:7` → `inbox(request)` →\n`current_customer(request)` → `inbox(): Ticket.objects.filter(...):14`\n\n- `request` enters from the public HTTP route.\n- `current_customer(request)` returns\n  `request.COOKIES.get(\"customer_key\", \"cst-north-loop\")`.\n- That returned string becomes the `customer_key` argument to\n  `Ticket.objects.filter(customer_key=current_customer(request))`.\n- The provided analysis found no auth decorator, ownership check, or validation on that\n  cookie value along this path.",
            "debateConsensus": "TP",
            "debateSummary": "- Provided transcript: **1** model argued true positive, **0** argued false positive.\n- The available reviewer reasoning stated that:\n  - `project/urls.py` mounts `portal.urls` at the site root\n  - `portal/urls.py:7` exposes `views.inbox`\n  - `inbox()` queries tickets by `current_customer(request)`\n  - `current_customer()` reads the cookie directly\n  - no decorator or in-view authorization check is present\n- The transcript also noted a possible counterargument that some upstream layer could\n  protect the route, but no such route-level control was identified in the supplied code.\n- Limitation: only one model transcript was provided, so the debate record is\n  effectively unchallenged even though the metadata reports consensus TP.",
