            "impact": "A caller can obtain ticket listings for the `customer_key` they supply, or for the\ndefault namespace `cst-north-loop` when no cookie is present. Based on the cited query,\nthis exposes up to the 50 most recently updated tickets for that tenant.",
            "prerequisites": "- The route must be reachable to an attacker; the reachability data marks it as a public\n  entry point.\n- `portal/urls.py` is part of the normal Django URL configuration, not an optional\n  extension in the provided evidence.\n- The trust boundary is between a network caller and tenant-scoped ticket data.\n- The attacker model is an unauthenticated user, or any user able to send `GET /` with\n  a chosen `customer_key` cookie or no cookie at all.\n- `AuthenticationMiddleware` is enabled per the context, but the supplied analysis found\n  no `login_required`, permission check, or ownership verification on this route.\n- The threat-model notes describe `Ticket.customer_key` as an authorization-critical\n  tenant discriminator and specifically call out lookups keyed only by this field as a\n  CWE-862 hotspot.\n- Related-known-pattern note: the supplied references include a CWE-862 knowledge-base\n  pattern, but no specific CVE was provided for this exact route.",
            "recommendation": {
              "codeAfter": "def current_customer(request):\n    if getattr(request.user, \"is_authenticated\", False):\n        return getattr(request.user, \"customer_key\", None)\n    return None\n\n\ndef inbox(request):\n    customer_key = current_customer(request)\n    if not customer_key:\n        return render(request, \"portal/inbox.html\", {\"tickets\": []}, status=403)\n    tickets = Ticket.objects.filter(customer_key=customer_key).order_by(\"-updated_at\")[:50]\n    return render(request, \"portal/inbox.html\", {\"tickets\": tickets, \"is_overdue\": is_overdue})",
