              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn portal/views.py, update the reply() ticket lookup at the get_object_or_404 call so it scopes the fetched Ticket by both id and current_customer(request) instead of id alone.\n\n### Suggested fix\ndef reply(request, ticket_id):\n    ticket = get_object_or_404(\n        Ticket,\n        id=ticket_id,\n        customer_key=current_customer(request),\n    )\n    form = ReplyForm(request.POST)\n    if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n        body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n        TicketNote.objects.create(ticket=ticket, author=form.cleaned_data[\"author\"], body=body)\n\n### Rationale\nFiltering the Ticket lookup by the request's authorized customer key enforces object-level access control before any note creation or status update occurs. Requests for a ticket outside that customer scope will fail the lookup, so the handler no longer applies writes to arbitrary tickets selected only by ID.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, send POST /tickets/<other_customer_ticket_id>/reply/ with valid author/body/status fields while presenting a different customer context; the handler creates a TicketNote and updates that ticket's status. After the change, the same request should return a not-found response and leave the other customer's Ticket and TicketNote records unchanged. A POST for a ticket owned by the current customer should still succeed.",
