 portal/services.py:28-31. DATA-FLOW: save_attachment stores upload.name and content via FileSystemStorage(location='media/uploads') with no route-level size or type restriction; together with project/urls.py:9 static MEDIA_URL serving, uploaded content becomes directly web-reachable in DEBUG deployments. PRECOND: The handler fetches Ticket(id=ticket_id) without customer/user scoping, so attackers can attach files to arbitrary tickets.\n    path(\"imports/\", views.imports, name=\"imports\"), # INDIRECT: Dispatches to views.imports(request: HttpRequest) at portal/views.py:77-82. TAINT: Uploaded request.FILES['bundle'] is attacker-controlled. DATA-FLOW: The route passes bundle to import_handoff(upload) at portal/services.py:34-51, which executes pickle.loads(upload.read()); this is a concrete unsafe-deserialization remote code execution sink (CWE-502). PRECOND: No login, staff, or permission check guards this bulk-import surface, making the deserialization sink anonymously reachable.\n]",
