            "cwe_display": "CWE-862: Missing Authorization",
            "cwe_name": "Missing Authorization",
            "dataFlowTrace": "`POST /tickets/<ticket_id>/attachments/` (`ticket_id`, uploaded `file`)  \n→ `portal/urls.py:<top-level>:12` dispatches to `upload_attachment(request, ticket_id)`  \n→ `portal/views.py:68-74` loads `ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)`  \n→ `portal/views.py:68-74` reads `form.cleaned_data[\"file\"]` from `request.FILES`  \n→ `portal/services.py:28-31` `save_attachment(ticket, upload)`  \n→ `Attachment.objects.create(ticket=ticket, original_name=upload.name, stored_name=name)`\n\nValidation checks on this path:\n- `request.method == \"POST\"` limits the HTTP verb only.\n- `form.is_valid()` checks that a file field is present and well-formed.\n- `get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)` checks existence only.\n- No check was found against `current_customer(request)`, `request.user`,\n  `ticket.customer_key`, or a permission decorator.",
            "debateConsensus": "TP",
            "debateSummary": "- **True positive:** 1 model\n- **False positive:** 0 models\n\nThe review transcript states that the route is reachable from the public URL map, the handler\nloads a `Ticket` solely by `id`, and the subsequent write associates the uploaded file with\nthat selected ticket. The counterpoints raised were CSRF enforcement and the need to know a\nvalid `ticket_id`; the reviewer treated those as access friction rather than object-level\nauthorization. No opposing model transcript was provided, so the consensus is based on a\nsingle-model review.",
            "end_line": 12,
            "fileSourceUrl": "https://github.com/caldova-io/support-portal/blob/1b68f887d82551e0d429c29bafbc3d11639c0700/portal/urls.py#L12",
            "firstDetected": "2026-08-20T05:18:44.943Z",
            "fixDiff": "--- a/portal/views.py\n+++ b/portal/views.py\n@@ -66,8 +66,10 @@\n \n \n def upload_attachment(request, ticket_id):\n-    ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n-    form = AttachmentForm(request.POST, request.FILES)\n+    ticket = get_object_or_404(\n+        Ticket, id=ticket_id, customer_key=current_customer(request)\n+    )\n+    form = AttachmentForm(request.POST, request.FILES)\n     if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n         save_attachment(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"file\"])\n         messages.success(request, \"Attachment stored.\")\n",
