            "dataFlowTrace": "`GET /tickets/search/?q=TERM` → `project/urls.py:<top-level>` → `portal/urls.py:<top-level>:9`\n→ `search(request)` in `portal/views.py:39-42` → `TicketSearch.find(term)` in\n`portal/services.py:11-20`\n\n- Entry variable: query parameter `q`\n- In `search(request)`: `term = request.GET.get(\"q\", \"\")`\n- Validation on path: only `if term else []`; empty strings are blocked, non-empty values pass\n- In `find(self, term)`: the same `term` is used to search `portal_ticket`\n- Reported query returns `id, reference, customer_name, subject, status, priority`\n- No route decorator, inline auth check, `has_perm`, or `current_customer(request)` call was\n  identified on this path\n- The reported SQL has no `customer_key = ...` predicate",
