              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn portal/urls.py, add the login_required import and wrap the search route at line 9 so anonymous requests cannot invoke views.search directly.\n\n### Suggested fix\nfrom django.contrib.auth.decorators import login_required\nfrom django.urls import path\nfrom . import views\n\napp_name = \"portal\"\nurlpatterns = [\n    path(\"\", views.inbox, name=\"inbox\"),\n    path(\"tickets/new/\", views.new_ticket, name=\"new_ticket\"),\n    path(\"tickets/search/\", login_required(views.search), name=\"search\"),\n    path(\"tickets/<int:ticket_id>/\", views.ticket_detail, name=\"ticket_detail\"),\n    path(\"tickets/<int:ticket_id>/reply/\", views.reply, name=\"reply\"),\n    path(\"tickets/<int:ticket_id>/attachments/\", views.upload_attachment, name=\"upload_attachment\"),\n\n### Rationale\nApplying login_required at route registration forces Django to perform an authentication check before dispatching to the search view. This removes the anonymous access path to the ticket search handler; tenant scoping in the view or service should still be reviewed separately.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, an unauthenticated GET to /tickets/search/?q=test reaches views.search and returns matching ticket metadata. After the change, the same unauthenticated request is redirected to the login flow or denied according to Django auth settings, while an authenticated request still reaches the handler.",
