              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn portal/views.py, update upload_attachment() at lines 68-74 to reject unauthenticated requests before loading the ticket or calling save_attachment().\n\n### Suggested fix\n    return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n\n\ndef upload_attachment(request, ticket_id):\n    if not request.user.is_authenticated:\n        messages.error(request, \"Login required.\")\n        return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket_id)\n\n    ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n    form = AttachmentForm(request.POST, request.FILES)\n    if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n        save_attachment(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"file\"])\n        messages.success(request, \"Attachment stored.\")\n    return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n\n\ndef imports(request):\n\n### Rationale\nChecking request.user.is_authenticated before the attachment write prevents anonymous callers from reaching the file-storage and Attachment creation path. This closes the missing-authentication condition by ensuring the state-changing operation is not available to unauthenticated requests.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, submit an unauthenticated POST with a valid CSRF token and multipart file data to /tickets/<existing_id>/attachments/ and observe that an Attachment row and stored file are created. After the change, repeat the same request and observe that no Attachment row is created, no file is stored, and the request is redirected back with the \"Login required.\" message.",
