            "severityRationale": "CVSS v3.1 base score 5.3 (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N, confidence: high) — AV:N (portal/urls.py:12 exposes upload_attachment on a network-reachable HTTP path and project/urls.py includes portal routes at the site root); AC:L (sending a POST with a chosen ticket_id and file is sufficient, and get_object_or_404 only requires that the target ticket exist); PR:N (portal/views.py:68-72 performs no login, ownership, or permission check before saving the attachment); UI:N (the attacker can drive the GET/POST flow and submit the multipart form without any separate victim action); S:U (the unauthorized write adds an attachment within the same portal application's ticket and attachment data store); C:N (this path writes data but does not directly expose ticket contents or other sensitive information to the attacker); I:L (portal/views.py:72 invokes save_attachment, which stores the uploaded file and creates an Attachment tied to the selected ticket, enabling unauthorized modification of stored ticket data); A:N (the demonstrated behavior is an unauthorized attachment write, not a direct availability loss).",
            "severitySource": "validator",
            "specificityGap": "[route-auth-gaps] project/urls.py:8 includes portal.urls directly, portal/urls.py:12 exposes upload_attachment, and portal/views.py:68-74 has no login_required/permission wrapper or in-function auth check. project/settings.py:22-30 only enables AuthenticationMiddleware, which populates request.user but does not require login. A remote user can therefore call this endpoint directly and cause save_attachment() to persist a file for any supplied ticket.",
            "summary": "`upload_attachment()` handles `POST /tickets/<ticket_id>/attachments/`, loads a `Ticket`\nby raw `ticket_id`, and passes an uploaded file to `save_attachment()`. The scanner flagged\nthat this write happens without a route-level or in-function authentication or permission\ncheck. This becomes a security issue if remote users can reach the route, obtain a valid\nCSRF token, and supply a `ticket_id` for a ticket they should not be allowed to modify.",
