            "impact": "A caller can cause stored ticket notes to appear under arbitrary names. This can affect the\nintegrity of ticket history, agent attribution, and any downstream display or workflow that treats\nthe `author` column as trustworthy identity data.\n\nThe supplied evidence does not show additional authorization decisions being made from\n`TicketNote.author`, so the observed effect is on stored identity metadata rather than on direct\nprivilege escalation.",
            "prerequisites": "- The endpoint is publicly reachable through:\n  - `portal/urls.py`: `path(\"tickets/<int:ticket_id>/reply/\", views.reply, name=\"reply\")`\n  - `project/urls.py`: includes `portal.urls`\n- No `login_required`, permission decorators, or equivalent guards were identified on `reply()`.\n- The code is part of the main Django view layer, not an optional or loadable extension.\n- The trust boundary is the HTTP request boundary into persisted `TicketNote` data.\n- The attacker is any client able to submit a POST request to this route; the broader question of\n  whether that client can reach arbitrary tickets is separate from this finding.\n- The issue depends on application semantics: if `TicketNote.author` is treated as an actor\n  identity, staff name, or audit field, the client controls that identity label.\n- The provided threat model's \"Agent note persistence\" boundary already identifies `author` and\n  `body` as user-influenced persisted fields.\n- The listed CVEs in the supplied threat material concern SQL injection, deserialization, path\n  traversal, request-boundary confusion, and XSS. None is a close match for this specific\n  note-author spoofing pattern.",
            "recommendation": {
              "codeAfter": "56: def reply(request, ticket_id):\n57:     ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n58:     form = ReplyForm(request.POST)\n59:     if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n60:         if not request.user.is_authenticated:\n61:             return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n62:         body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n63:         TicketNote.objects.create(\n64:             ticket=ticket,\n65:             author=request.user.get_username(),\n66:             body=body,\n67:         )\n68:         ticket.status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"]\n69:         ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"])\n70:         messages.success(request, \"Response added.\")\n71:     return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)",
              "codeBefore": "56: def reply(request, ticket_id):\n57:     ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n58:     form = ReplyForm(request.POST)\n59:     if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n60:         body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n61:         TicketNote.objects.create(ticket=ticket, author=form.cleaned_data[\"author\"], body=body)\n62:         ticket.status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"]\n63:         ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"])\n64:         messages.success(request, \"Response added.\")\n65:     return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)",
              "fixDiff": "--- a/portal/views.py\n+++ b/portal/views.py\n@@ -56,11 +56,17 @@\n def reply(request, ticket_id):\n     ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n     form = ReplyForm(request.POST)\n-    if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n-        body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n-        TicketNote.objects.create(ticket=ticket, author=form.cleaned_data[\"author\"], body=body)\n-        ticket.status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"]\n-        ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"])\n+    if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n+        if not request.user.is_authenticated:\n+            return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n+        body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n+        TicketNote.objects.create(\n+            ticket=ticket,\n+            author=request.user.get_username(),\n+            body=body,\n+        )\n+        ticket.status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"]\n+        ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"])\n         messages.success(request, \"Response added.\")\n     return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn portal/views.py, update reply() at lines 59-63 so the note author is not read from form.cleaned_data[\"author\"]. Require an authenticated user for reply submission and populate TicketNote.author from request.user.get_username() instead of the POST field.\n\n### Suggested fix\ndef reply(request, ticket_id):\n    ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n    form = ReplyForm(request.POST)\n    if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n        if not request.user.is_authenticated:\n            return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n        body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n        TicketNote.objects.create(\n            ticket=ticket,\n            author=request.user.get_username(),\n            body=body,\n        )\n        ticket.status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"]\n        ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"])\n        messages.success(request, \"Response added.\")\n    return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n\n### Rationale\nThis change removes the client-controlled author field from the authoritative write path. The stored author value is derived from server-side authentication state, so the caller can no longer choose an arbitrary agent or user name in the persisted note metadata.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, submit POST /tickets/<ticket_id>/reply/ with author=Alice while authenticated as a different user or without authentication; the created TicketNote stores author='Alice'. After the change, the same request should either be rejected/redirected when unauthenticated or create the note with author set to the authenticated user's username, regardless of the submitted author field.",
              "remediationSteps": {
                "description": "In portal/views.py, update reply() at lines 59-63 so the note author is not read from form.cleaned_data[\"author\"]. Require an authenticated user for reply submission and populate TicketNote.author from request.user.get_username() instead of the POST field.",
                "rational": "This change removes the client-controlled author field from the authoritative write path. The stored author value is derived from server-side authentication state, so the caller can no longer choose an arbitrary agent or user name in the persisted note metadata.",
                "rationale": "This change removes the client-controlled author field from the authoritative write path. The stored author value is derived from server-side authentication state, so the caller can no longer choose an arbitrary agent or user name in the persisted note metadata.",
                "suggestedFix": "def reply(request, ticket_id):\n    ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n    form = ReplyForm(request.POST)\n    if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n        if not request.user.is_authenticated:\n            return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n        body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n        TicketNote.objects.create(\n            ticket=ticket,\n            author=request.user.get_username(),\n            body=body,\n        )\n        ticket.status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"]\n        ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"])\n        messages.success(request, \"Response added.\")\n    return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)",
                "verification": "Before the change, submit POST /tickets/<ticket_id>/reply/ with author=Alice while authenticated as a different user or without authentication; the created TicketNote stores author='Alice'. After the change, the same request should either be rejected/redirected when unauthenticated or create the note with author set to the authenticated user's username, regardless of the submitted author field."
              }
