            "impact": "A requester can create a ticket row under another `customer_key` value. If downstream listing,\nrouting, search, or reporting logic treats `customer_key` as the customer namespace, the new\nrecord can be attributed to the wrong tenant. The provided evidence covers record creation and\nmisattribution; it does not by itself show unauthorized read, update, or deletion of existing\ntickets.",
            "prerequisites": "- The handler is externally reachable through `portal/urls.py:8` at `tickets/new/`.\n- This is normal application code in a network-facing Django service, not an optional or\n  loadable extension.\n- The finding matters if `customer_key` is a trust boundary for tenant ownership or routing.\n  The repository provides supporting context for that interpretation:\n  - `inbox()` filters tickets with\n    `Ticket.objects.filter(customer_key=current_customer(request))` at `portal/views.py:14`.\n  - The threat model describes `Ticket.customer_key` as an authorization-critical tenant\n    discriminator.\n- The attacker model is an external submitter able to send a valid POST request; no in-repo\n  caller or extra lifecycle step is required.\n- `current_customer()` currently reads `request.COOKIES[\"customer_key\"]`, which is also\n  client-controlled and does not provide a server-side authorization check.\n- The supplied CVE references in the threat model cover other classes such as SQL injection,\n  path traversal, and request parsing issues; no direct CVE mapping for this exact pattern was\n  provided.",
            "recommendation": {
              "codeAfter": "6: from .workflow import allowed_statuses, is_overdue, priority_for, response_due_at\n7:\n8:\n9: def current_customer(request):\n10:     return request.session.get(\"customer_key\")\n11:\n12:\n13: def inbox(request):\n// ...\n17:\n18: def new_ticket(request):\n19:     if request.method == \"POST\":\n20:         form = TicketForm(request.POST)\n21:         if form.is_valid():\n22:             customer_key = current_customer(request)\n23:             if not customer_key:\n24:                 form.add_error(\"customer_key\", \"Customer context unavailable.\")\n25:             else:\n26:                 data = form.cleaned_data\n27:                 ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n28:                     reference=f\"RB-{Ticket.objects.count() + 1001}\",\n29:                     customer_key=customer_key,\n30:                     customer_name=data[\"customer_name\"],\n31:                     delivery_address=data[\"delivery_address\"],\n32:                     robot_unit=data[\"robot_unit\"],\n33:                     subject=data[\"subject\"],\n34:                     description=data[\"description\"],\n35:                     priority=priority_for(data[\"subject\"], data[\"description\"]),\n36:                 )\n37:                 return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n38:     else:\n39:         form = TicketForm(initial={\"customer_key\": current_customer(request)})\n40:     return render(request, \"portal/new_ticket.html\", {\"form\": form})",
              "codeBefore": "6: from .workflow import allowed_statuses, is_overdue, priority_for, response_due_at\n7:\n8:\n9: def current_customer(request):\n10:     return request.COOKIES.get(\"customer_key\", \"cst-north-loop\")\n11:\n12:\n13: def inbox(request):\n// ...\n17:\n18: def new_ticket(request):\n19:     if request.method == \"POST\":\n20:         form = TicketForm(request.POST)\n21:         if form.is_valid():\n22:             data = form.cleaned_data\n23:             ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n24:                 reference=f\"RB-{Ticket.objects.count() + 1001}\",\n25:                 customer_key=data[\"customer_key\"],\n26:                 customer_name=data[\"customer_name\"],\n27:                 delivery_address=data[\"delivery_address\"],\n28:                 robot_unit=data[\"robot_unit\"],\n29:                 subject=data[\"subject\"],\n30:                 description=data[\"description\"],\n31:                 priority=priority_for(data[\"subject\"], data[\"description\"]),\n32:             )\n33:             return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n34:     else:\n35:         form = TicketForm(initial={\"customer_key\": current_customer(request)})\n36:     return render(request, \"portal/new_ticket.html\", {\"form\": form})",
              "fixDiff": "--- a/portal/views.py\n+++ b/portal/views.py\n@@ -6,8 +6,8 @@\n from .workflow import allowed_statuses, is_overdue, priority_for, response_due_at\n \n \n-def current_customer(request):\n-    return request.COOKIES.get(\"customer_key\", \"cst-north-loop\")\n+def current_customer(request):\n+    return request.session.get(\"customer_key\")\n \n \n def inbox(request):\n@@ -17,20 +17,24 @@\n \n def new_ticket(request):\n     if request.method == \"POST\":\n-        form = TicketForm(request.POST)\n-        if form.is_valid():\n-            data = form.cleaned_data\n-            ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n-                reference=f\"RB-{Ticket.objects.count() + 1001}\",\n-                customer_key=data[\"customer_key\"],\n-                customer_name=data[\"customer_name\"],\n-                delivery_address=data[\"delivery_address\"],\n-                robot_unit=data[\"robot_unit\"],\n-                subject=data[\"subject\"],\n-                description=data[\"description\"],\n-                priority=priority_for(data[\"subject\"], data[\"description\"]),\n-            )\n-            return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n+        form = TicketForm(request.POST)\n+        if form.is_valid():\n+            customer_key = current_customer(request)\n+            if not customer_key:\n+                form.add_error(\"customer_key\", \"Customer context unavailable.\")\n+            else:\n+                data = form.cleaned_data\n+                ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n+                    reference=f\"RB-{Ticket.objects.count() + 1001}\",\n+                    customer_key=customer_key,\n+                    customer_name=data[\"customer_name\"],\n+                    delivery_address=data[\"delivery_address\"],\n+                    robot_unit=data[\"robot_unit\"],\n+                    subject=data[\"subject\"],\n+                    description=data[\"description\"],\n+                    priority=priority_for(data[\"subject\"], data[\"description\"]),\n+                )\n+                return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n     else:\n         form = TicketForm(initial={\"customer_key\": current_customer(request)})\n     return render(request, \"portal/new_ticket.html\", {\"form\": form})",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn portal/views.py, change current_customer() to read the tenant key from server-side session state instead of an unsigned cookie, and in new_ticket() at lines 20-33 ignore the posted customer_key and write Ticket.customer_key from current_customer(request), returning a form error when no trusted customer context exists.\n\n### Suggested fix\nfrom .workflow import allowed_statuses, is_overdue, priority_for, response_due_at\n\n\ndef current_customer(request):\n    return request.session.get(\"customer_key\")\n\n\ndef inbox(request):\n\ndef new_ticket(request):\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\n        form = TicketForm(request.POST)\n        if form.is_valid():\n            customer_key = current_customer(request)\n            if not customer_key:\n                form.add_error(\"customer_key\", \"Customer context unavailable.\")\n            else:\n                data = form.cleaned_data\n                ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n                    reference=f\"RB-{Ticket.objects.count() + 1001}\",\n                    customer_key=customer_key,\n                    customer_name=data[\"customer_name\"],\n                    delivery_address=data[\"delivery_address\"],\n                    robot_unit=data[\"robot_unit\"],\n                    subject=data[\"subject\"],\n                    description=data[\"description\"],\n                    priority=priority_for(data[\"subject\"], data[\"description\"]),\n                )\n                return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n    else:\n        form = TicketForm(initial={\"customer_key\": current_customer(request)})\n    return render(request, \"portal/new_ticket.html\", {\"form\": form})\n\n### Rationale\nThe fix removes tenant identity from attacker-controlled inputs. Reading customer_key from server-side session state and assigning that value during Ticket.objects.create() binds the new ticket to application-controlled context, so a submitted form field cannot select another customer's namespace.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, submit POST /tickets/new/ with customer_key=cst-victim while the browser has either no tenant session or a different tenant context; the created Ticket row stores cst-victim. After the change, the same POST should either store the session-bound customer_key instead of cst-victim, or fail validation with \"Customer context unavailable.\" when no trusted tenant context is present.",
              "remediationSteps": {
                "description": "In portal/views.py, change current_customer() to read the tenant key from server-side session state instead of an unsigned cookie, and in new_ticket() at lines 20-33 ignore the posted customer_key and write Ticket.customer_key from current_customer(request), returning a form error when no trusted customer context exists.",
                "rational": "The fix removes tenant identity from attacker-controlled inputs. Reading customer_key from server-side session state and assigning that value during Ticket.objects.create() binds the new ticket to application-controlled context, so a submitted form field cannot select another customer's namespace.",
                "rationale": "The fix removes tenant identity from attacker-controlled inputs. Reading customer_key from server-side session state and assigning that value during Ticket.objects.create() binds the new ticket to application-controlled context, so a submitted form field cannot select another customer's namespace.",
                "suggestedFix": "from .workflow import allowed_statuses, is_overdue, priority_for, response_due_at\n\n\ndef current_customer(request):\n    return request.session.get(\"customer_key\")\n\n\ndef inbox(request):\n\ndef new_ticket(request):\n    if request.method == \"POST\":\n        form = TicketForm(request.POST)\n        if form.is_valid():\n            customer_key = current_customer(request)\n            if not customer_key:\n                form.add_error(\"customer_key\", \"Customer context unavailable.\")\n            else:\n                data = form.cleaned_data\n                ticket = Ticket.objects.create(\n                    reference=f\"RB-{Ticket.objects.count() + 1001}\",\n                    customer_key=customer_key,\n                    customer_name=data[\"customer_name\"],\n                    delivery_address=data[\"delivery_address\"],\n                    robot_unit=data[\"robot_unit\"],\n                    subject=data[\"subject\"],\n                    description=data[\"description\"],\n                    priority=priority_for(data[\"subject\"], data[\"description\"]),\n                )\n                return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n    else:\n        form = TicketForm(initial={\"customer_key\": current_customer(request)})\n    return render(request, \"portal/new_ticket.html\", {\"form\": form})",
                "verification": "Before the change, submit POST /tickets/new/ with customer_key=cst-victim while the browser has either no tenant session or a different tenant context; the created Ticket row stores cst-victim. After the change, the same POST should either store the session-bound customer_key instead of cst-victim, or fail validation with \"Customer context unavailable.\" when no trusted tenant context is present."
