            "annotatedSource": "def reply(request, ticket_id): # TAINT: request and ticket_id are untrusted HTTP inputs to a state-changing endpoint PRECOND: portal/urls.py:11 exposes direct POST access with no authentication or permission wrapper HIST: portal/views.py is ranked a primary request boundary with CWE-20, CWE-862, and CWE-79 risk\n    ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id) # PRECOND: missing ownership check against ticket.customer_key/current_customer(); guessed ids let an attacker target another customer's ticket DATA-FLOW: get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id) enforces existence only, turning sequential ids into an IDOR write target\n    form = ReplyForm(request.POST) # TAINT: request.POST is attacker-controlled input to ReplyForm CONSTRAINT: ReplyForm only enforces author<=80, status in {open, waiting, resolved}, and leaves body unbounded in forms.py:13-16\n    if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid(): # PRECOND: form.is_valid() does not enforce workflow.allowed_statuses(ticket.status); any of the three statuses is accepted regardless of current state\n        body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request) # TAINT: form.cleaned_data[\"body\"] remains attacker-controlled text DATA-FLOW: render_agent_response() in services.py:23-25 compiles the user body as django.template.Template with {ticket, agent=request.user, request}, enabling server-side template evaluation and disclosure of server-context data into the stored note\n        TicketNote.objects.create(ticket=ticket, author=form.cleaned_data[\"author\"], body=body) # DATA-FLOW: rendered body and tainted author are persisted in TicketNote (models.py:25-29) for the selected ticket ERRPATH: this insert occurs before line 63, so a later save failure leaves a note committed while ticket.status stays stale\n        ticket.status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"] # TAINT: posted status is written directly to Ticket.status INV: the workflow state machine can be bypassed here: workflow.STEPS forbids resolved→* but the server trusts any ReplyForm choice\n        ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"]) # DATA-FLOW: the unauthorized status change is persisted to the database ERRPATH: no transaction spans lines 61-63, so note creation and status update can commit inconsistently\n        messages.success(request, \"Response added.\")\n    return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)",
