            "function": "portal/views.py:reply",
            "impact": "A requester who can reach this endpoint can move tickets into states that the defined workflow\ndoes not allow, such as changing a `resolved` ticket back to `open` or `waiting`. If other\nlogic, reporting, or access decisions depend on ticket status, those behaviors would then act\non the unauthorized state.",
            "prerequisites": "- The endpoint must be reachable by an actor who can send a POST to\n  `/tickets/<ticket_id>/reply/`.\n- This code is part of the main Django view layer, not an optional or loadable extension.\n- The trust boundary is the HTTP request boundary: client-supplied form data controls a\n  workflow state written to persistence.\n- The current implementation treats workflow enforcement as a UI/display concern:\n  `ticket_detail()` passes `allowed_statuses(ticket.status)` to the template, but `reply()`\n  does not enforce it server-side.\n- The provided threat-model context notes that `Ticket.status` relies on application-level\n  choices rather than DB constraints, which is consistent with this pattern.\n- The listed CVEs in the provided context do not include a directly analogous workflow\n  transition issue.",
            "recommendation": {
              "codeAfter": "56: def reply(request, ticket_id):\n57:     ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n58:     form = ReplyForm(request.POST)\n59:     if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n60:         new_status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"]\n61:         if new_status != ticket.status and new_status not in allowed_statuses(ticket.status):\n62:             return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n63:         body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n64:         TicketNote.objects.create(ticket=ticket, author=form.cleaned_data[\"author\"], body=body)\n65:         ticket.status = new_status\n66:         ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"])\n67:         messages.success(request, \"Response added.\")\n68:     return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)",
              "codeBefore": "56: def reply(request, ticket_id):\n57:     ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n58:     form = ReplyForm(request.POST)\n59:     if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n60:         body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n61:         TicketNote.objects.create(ticket=ticket, author=form.cleaned_data[\"author\"], body=body)\n62:         ticket.status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"]\n63:         ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"])\n64:         messages.success(request, \"Response added.\")\n65:     return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)",
              "fixDiff": "--- a/portal/views.py\n+++ b/portal/views.py\n@@ -56,12 +56,15 @@\n def reply(request, ticket_id):\n     ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n     form = ReplyForm(request.POST)\n-    if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n-        body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n-        TicketNote.objects.create(ticket=ticket, author=form.cleaned_data[\"author\"], body=body)\n-        ticket.status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"]\n-        ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"])\n-        messages.success(request, \"Response added.\")\n+    if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n+        new_status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"]\n+        if new_status != ticket.status and new_status not in allowed_statuses(ticket.status):\n+            return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n+        body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n+        TicketNote.objects.create(ticket=ticket, author=form.cleaned_data[\"author\"], body=body)\n+        ticket.status = new_status\n+        ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"])\n+        messages.success(request, \"Response added.\")\n     return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn portal/views.py, update reply() around lines 59-64 to validate the submitted status against allowed_statuses(ticket.status) before creating the note and saving ticket.status, and only persist the change when the transition is permitted or unchanged.\n\n### Suggested fix\ndef reply(request, ticket_id):\n    ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n    form = ReplyForm(request.POST)\n    if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n        new_status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"]\n        if new_status != ticket.status and new_status not in allowed_statuses(ticket.status):\n            return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n        body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n        TicketNote.objects.create(ticket=ticket, author=form.cleaned_data[\"author\"], body=body)\n        ticket.status = new_status\n        ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"])\n        messages.success(request, \"Response added.\")\n    return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n\n### Rationale\nChecking the requested status against the workflow helper on the server side enforces the same transition rules regardless of client-side UI state. Treating the submitted value as valid only when it matches the current state or an allowed next state prevents forbidden transitions such as resolved-to-open from being written to the database.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, submit POST /tickets/<id>/reply/ for a ticket whose current status is resolved with form field status=open; the note is stored and the ticket status changes to open. After the change, the same request should return without changing ticket.status from resolved. Also verify that a permitted transition, such as open to waiting, still updates the ticket successfully.",
