              "description": {
                "text": "### Description\nIn portal/views.py, update reply() around lines 59-64 to validate the submitted status against allowed_statuses(ticket.status) before creating the note and saving ticket.status, and only persist the change when the transition is permitted or unchanged.\n\n### Suggested fix\ndef reply(request, ticket_id):\n    ticket = get_object_or_404(Ticket, id=ticket_id)\n    form = ReplyForm(request.POST)\n    if request.method == \"POST\" and form.is_valid():\n        new_status = form.cleaned_data[\"status\"]\n        if new_status != ticket.status and new_status not in allowed_statuses(ticket.status):\n            return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n        body = render_agent_response(ticket, form.cleaned_data[\"body\"], request)\n        TicketNote.objects.create(ticket=ticket, author=form.cleaned_data[\"author\"], body=body)\n        ticket.status = new_status\n        ticket.save(update_fields=[\"status\", \"updated_at\"])\n        messages.success(request, \"Response added.\")\n    return redirect(\"portal:ticket_detail\", ticket_id=ticket.id)\n\n### Rationale\nChecking the requested status against the workflow helper on the server side enforces the same transition rules regardless of client-side UI state. Treating the submitted value as valid only when it matches the current state or an allowed next state prevents forbidden transitions such as resolved-to-open from being written to the database.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, submit POST /tickets/<id>/reply/ for a ticket whose current status is resolved with form field status=open; the note is stored and the ticket status changes to open. After the change, the same request should return without changing ticket.status from resolved. Also verify that a permitted transition, such as open to waiting, still updates the ticket successfully."
              }
