              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn portal/workflow.py, replace priority_for() at lines 25-31 so ticket creation no longer derives and persists 'high' or 'urgent' priority from requester-controlled subject/description text alone.\n\n### Suggested fix\n    return [STEPS[name] for name in step.next_steps]\n\n\ndef priority_for(subject, description):\n    return \"normal\"\n\n\ndef response_due_at(ticket):\n\n### Rationale\nReturning a neutral default removes the direct path from untrusted free text to the persisted Ticket.priority workflow state. This prevents requester-supplied keywords from being treated as authoritative escalation data for downstream SLA calculations.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, submit a new ticket with subject or description containing words such as 'refund', 'stuck', 'late', 'cold', or 'spill' and observe that the stored priority becomes 'high' or 'urgent' and response_due_at() uses the shorter deadline. After the change, submit the same inputs and observe that the stored priority remains 'normal' and response_due_at() uses the normal deadline unless some separate trusted workflow updates the priority.",
