            "dataFlowTrace": "- `project/wsgi.py:<top-level>` or `project/asgi.py:<top-level>`\n  → sets `DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=\"project.settings\"`\n- `django.core.wsgi.get_wsgi_application()` / `django.core.asgi.get_asgi_application()`\n  → imports `project.settings`\n- `project/settings.py:<top-level>:8`\n  → `SECRET_KEY` receives either:\n  - `DJANGO_SECRET_KEY` from environment / `.env`, or\n  - fallback literal `\"caldova-local-support-key\"`\n- Django request processing\n  → middleware and framework signing code use `settings.SECRET_KEY`\n  when generating or validating signed artifacts from HTTP requests/responses\n\n**Variables and checks**\n- Input variable: `DJANGO_SECRET_KEY`\n- Derived state: `SECRET_KEY`\n- Validation: no code-level check requires the variable to be present; the fallback is\n  accepted unconditionally",
