            "debateSummary": "- **True positive:** 1 model\n- **False positive:** 0 models\n\nThe review transcript states that the fallback literal places the application in an\ninsecure default state when `DJANGO_SECRET_KEY` is unset, and that Django uses this key\nfor signing-related features. The same review also noted a limitation: the repository\ndoes not, by itself, demonstrate every example impact in the scanner text, such as\nsigned-cookie session impersonation, because the session backend and custom signing usage\nare not shown. This was a single-model review, so there was no multi-model disagreement\nrecorded.",
