            "summary": "`project/settings.py` initializes Django's `SECRET_KEY` from `DJANGO_SECRET_KEY`, but it\nfalls back to the literal `\"caldova-local-support-key\"` when the environment variable\nis absent. The scanner flagged this as a hard-coded cryptographic key because Django uses\n`SECRET_KEY` for signing and integrity features. This becomes a security issue if a\ndeployment starts without `DJANGO_SECRET_KEY` set and then accepts Django-signed\nartifacts from untrusted clients.",
