            "dataFlowTrace": "- `project/wsgi.py` / `project/asgi.py` → Django startup import of\n  `project.settings` → `<top-level>:9`\n  - `os.getenv(\"DJANGO_DEBUG\", \"1\")` reads environment variable `DJANGO_DEBUG`\n  - If unset, fallback value `\"1\"` is used\n  - Expression result is assigned to `DEBUG`\n  - No code-level check forces `False` on the unset path\n\n- Public exception path shown by reachability analysis:\n  - `portal/views.py:imports(request)` → `import_handoff(upload)` →\n    `pickle.loads(upload.read())`\n  - Variable flow: `request.FILES[\"bundle\"]` → `upload` → `upload.read()`\n  - Validation: route checks request method and file presence, but not file\n    contents before deserialization\n  - A malformed upload can raise an unhandled exception, after which Django uses\n    `settings.DEBUG` from `project/settings.py:9` to choose the error response\n\n- Additional corroborating path from source:\n  - `portal/views.py:search(request)` → `TicketSearch().find(term)` →\n    `cursor.execute(sql)`\n  - Variable flow: `request.GET[\"q\"]` → `term` → interpolated SQL string\n  - Validation: only truthiness is checked before the query path",
