            "function": "project/settings.py:<top-level>",
            "impact": "A requester who triggers an unhandled exception can receive Django's technical\ndebug response instead of the generic error page. That response can include stack\ntraces, source locations, environment and settings-derived diagnostics, and\nother implementation details that may assist follow-on attacks.",
            "prerequisites": "- `DJANGO_DEBUG` must be unset, or set to a value that makes the expression at\n  line 9 evaluate to `True`.\n- The application must be running in a network-accessible deployment where\n  requesters can reach routes that can raise unhandled exceptions.\n- This code is in the main `project/settings.py` module, which is loaded by both\n  `project/wsgi.py` and `project/asgi.py`; it is not an optional extension.\n- The trust boundary crossed is remote HTTP input to server-side exception\n  rendering. The attacker is an external requester who already has network\n  access to application endpoints.\n- Django's technical debug page is by-design framework behavior when\n  `DEBUG=True`; the flagged condition is the application's default configuration,\n  not an unexpected framework action.\n- The listed CVE references in the threat-model material concern SQL injection,\n  deserialization, traversal, and request parsing patterns. None directly match\n  this debug-default configuration issue.",
            "recommendation": {
              "codeAfter": "5: BASE_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n6: load_dotenv(BASE_DIR / \".env\")\n7:\n8: SECRET_KEY = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_SECRET_KEY\", \"caldova-local-support-key\")\n9: DEBUG = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_DEBUG\", \"0\").strip().lower() in {\"1\", \"true\", \"yes\", \"on\"}\n10: ALLOWED_HOSTS = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS\", \"127.0.0.1,localhost\").split(\",\")\n11:\n12: INSTALLED_APPS = [\n13:     \"django.contrib.admin\",",
