              "fixDiff": "--- a/project/settings.py\n+++ b/project/settings.py\n@@ -5,9 +5,9 @@\n BASE_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n load_dotenv(BASE_DIR / \".env\")\n \n-SECRET_KEY = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_SECRET_KEY\", \"caldova-local-support-key\")\n-DEBUG = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_DEBUG\", \"1\") == \"1\"\n-ALLOWED_HOSTS = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS\", \"127.0.0.1,localhost\").split(\",\")\n+SECRET_KEY = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_SECRET_KEY\", \"caldova-local-support-key\")\n+DEBUG = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_DEBUG\", \"0\").strip().lower() in {\"1\", \"true\", \"yes\", \"on\"}\n+ALLOWED_HOSTS = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS\", \"127.0.0.1,localhost\").split(\",\")\n \n INSTALLED_APPS = [\n     \"django.contrib.admin\",",
              "remediationBackwardCompat": "### Description\nIn project/settings.py at module top-level line 9, change the DEBUG assignment so an unset DJANGO_DEBUG defaults to False instead of True, while still accepting explicit truthy values such as 1/true/yes/on.\n\n### Suggested fix\nBASE_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nload_dotenv(BASE_DIR / \".env\")\n\nSECRET_KEY = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_SECRET_KEY\", \"caldova-local-support-key\")\nDEBUG = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_DEBUG\", \"0\").strip().lower() in {\"1\", \"true\", \"yes\", \"on\"}\nALLOWED_HOSTS = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS\", \"127.0.0.1,localhost\").split(\",\")\n\nINSTALLED_APPS = [\n    \"django.contrib.admin\",\n\n### Rationale\nThis change removes the unsafe default path that enables Django's technical debug responses when DJANGO_DEBUG is absent. Requiring an explicit truthy environment value keeps debug behavior opt-in, so ordinary deployments do not expose stack traces and settings-derived diagnostics by omission.\n\n### Verification\nBefore the change, start the app with DJANGO_DEBUG unset and send a request that triggers an unhandled exception, such as a malformed upload to /imports/; the response uses Django debug output because DEBUG evaluates to True. After the change, repeat the same test with DJANGO_DEBUG unset and the response should be the non-debug error page; setting DJANGO_DEBUG=1 should still enable debug behavior intentionally.",
              "remediationSteps": {
                "description": "In project/settings.py at module top-level line 9, change the DEBUG assignment so an unset DJANGO_DEBUG defaults to False instead of True, while still accepting explicit truthy values such as 1/true/yes/on.",
                "rational": "This change removes the unsafe default path that enables Django's technical debug responses when DJANGO_DEBUG is absent. Requiring an explicit truthy environment value keeps debug behavior opt-in, so ordinary deployments do not expose stack traces and settings-derived diagnostics by omission.",
                "rationale": "This change removes the unsafe default path that enables Django's technical debug responses when DJANGO_DEBUG is absent. Requiring an explicit truthy environment value keeps debug behavior opt-in, so ordinary deployments do not expose stack traces and settings-derived diagnostics by omission.",
                "suggestedFix": "BASE_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nload_dotenv(BASE_DIR / \".env\")\n\nSECRET_KEY = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_SECRET_KEY\", \"caldova-local-support-key\")\nDEBUG = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_DEBUG\", \"0\").strip().lower() in {\"1\", \"true\", \"yes\", \"on\"}\nALLOWED_HOSTS = os.getenv(\"DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS\", \"127.0.0.1,localhost\").split(\",\")\n\nINSTALLED_APPS = [\n    \"django.contrib.admin\",",
                "verification": "Before the change, start the app with DJANGO_DEBUG unset and send a request that triggers an unhandled exception, such as a malformed upload to /imports/; the response uses Django debug output because DEBUG evaluates to True. After the change, repeat the same test with DJANGO_DEBUG unset and the response should be the non-debug error page; setting DJANGO_DEBUG=1 should still enable debug behavior intentionally."
              }
