            "cwe_display": "CWE-362: Concurrent Execution using Shared Resource with Improper Synchronization ('Race Condition')",
            "cwe_name": "Concurrent Execution using Shared Resource with Improper Synchronization ('Race Condition')",
            "dataFlowTrace": "- `HTTP POST /tickets/new/` → `new_ticket(request)` → `new_ticket():24`\n  - `request.POST` flows into `form = TicketForm(request.POST)` at line 20.\n  - `form.is_valid()` validates submitted fields, then `data = form.cleaned_data` at line 22.\n  - `reference` does **not** come from a user field; it is computed inline from shared database\n    state as `Ticket.objects.count() + 1001` at line 24.\n  - That computed value is passed directly as the `reference` argument to\n    `Ticket.objects.create(...)` at lines 23-32.\n  - No `transaction.atomic`, row/table lock, sequence, retry loop, or exception handling is\n    present around the `count()` plus `create()` pair.\n\n- Concurrent writer path affecting the same state:\n  - `HTTP request` → `imports()` → `import_handoff()` → `Ticket.objects.create(...)`\n  - This separate entry point also inserts `Ticket` rows, so it can change the table count between\n    the read in `new_ticket()` and the later insert.",
            "debateConsensus": "TP",
            "debateSummary": "- Review outcome in the supplied data: **1 true-positive assessment, 0 false-positive\n  assessments**.\n- The available reviewer argued that `count()` and `create()` are separate operations with no\n  synchronization, so two concurrent requests can derive the same `reference` and one insert can\n  fail on the unique constraint.\n- The main caveat raised was that some databases serialize writes and collisions may be\n  infrequent; the review still noted that this does not remove the race between the earlier\n  `COUNT(*)` read and the later `INSERT`.\n- This finding was not accompanied by a multi-model disagreement record; the debate data provided\n  here is effectively single-reviewer, which limits cross-review comparison.\n- The related known pattern supplied for this finding is the generic CWE-362 TOCTOU class, not a\n  project-specific CVE variant.",
            "end_line": 24,
            "fileSourceUrl": "https://github.com/caldova-io/support-portal/blob/1b68f887d82551e0d429c29bafbc3d11639c0700/portal/views.py#L24",
